WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Governments keep changing
taxes on company profits.

2
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.580
The United States cut
its main rate from 35

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.540
per cent to 21.

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.310
The UK cut its rate to 19 per cent,

5
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.470
then raised it to 25.

6
00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:17.160
Supporters of lower rates
say firms will invest more.

7
00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.350
But will they?

8
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.270
So how can a government raise
the most its economy can produce,

9
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.380
and why does it take so long?

10
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.380
In this mission, you'll see
what changes on the graph

11
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.850
when an economy's capacity changes.

12
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.130
Then you'll build roads and
broadband in a graph lab,

13
00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.840
and compare the short
run with the long run.

14
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.720
Your mission: find out which
policies can raise capacity,

15
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.950
and why they take years to pay off.
